{
  "ai": {
    "chunks": [
      "Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Mu'adhi narrated to us. He said: Ahmad ibn Haywayh al-Jurjani al-Mudhakkir narrated to us. He said: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Bilal narrated to us. He said: Abu Muhammad narrated to us. He said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Karram narrated to us. He said: Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us. He said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us. He said: Mu'awiya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr.",
      "He said: I asked Ibn Abbas: What will be given to one who fasts the month of Ramadan and recognizes its right? He said: Prepare - O Ibn Jubayr - so that I may tell you something that your ears have never heard and that has never come to your heart. Empty yourself for what you have asked me about, for what you wanted is the knowledge of the ancients and the later ones.",
      "Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: So I left him and prepared for the next day. I went early at dawn, prayed the dawn prayer, then mentioned the hadith. He turned his face toward me and said: Listen to what I say: I heard the Messenger of God (may blessings be upon him and his family) say: If you were to know what you have in Ramadan you would increase your thanksgiving to God. On the first night, God forgave all the sins of my Nation, raised you by two million ranks, and built fifty cities for you.",
      "On the second through tenth days, God records for every step the worship of a year and the reward of a prophet; gives domes of pearl in Paradise with houses of light; palaces in the Paradise of Eternity with heavenly maidens; cities in the Paradise of Refuge with tablespreads of food; cities in the Abode of Peace with beds of gold and spouses from the houris; the reward of martyrs and saints; the deeds of worshipers and ascetics; the gifts of scholars and retreaters; the fulfillment of seventy thousand needs with all creation seeking forgiveness for you.",
      "On the eleventh through twentieth days: the reward of four pilgrimages and Umras; sins changed to good deeds multiplied a million times; the worship of the people of Mecca and Medina; meeting the prophets Adam, Nuh, Ibrahim, Musa, Dawud, and Sulayman; fulfillment of needs and forty lights on the Day of Resurrection; garments and a she-camel from the grave; divine forgiveness for them and their fathers; angels ordered to seek forgiveness until the following year; all angels in heaven and earth visit your graves; seventy thousand protective angels, a trench between you and the Fire, the reward of reciting all scriptures, and a thousand houris for every Quran verse.",
      "On the twenty-first day through the twenty-fifth day: the grave widened, faces like Yusuf's; the Angel of Death comes gently as to the prophets; crossing the Path with the prophets and saints; seeing your place in Paradise and the reward of freeing slaves; green domes beneath the Throne where God says: O Nation of Muhammad! I am your Lord; be shaded by My Throne, eat and drink, neither fear nor grieve. By My glory, I will crown you with light and mount you on she-camels of light to enter Paradise without reckoning.",
      "On the twenty-sixth day through the completion of thirty days: God forgives all sins except bloodshed and wealth; as though you supported every believer and recited every revealed book; cities of light, palaces of silver, chambers, and beds of pearl in the various Paradises; a million locales with domes and heavenly maidens. When thirty days are complete, God records the reward of a thousand martyrs and saints for every day, the worship of fifty years, raises your rank by the Nile's length, records dissociation from the Fire, a permit on the Path, and safety from punishment. In Paradise is the gate al-Rayyan, opened only for fasting men and women. Ridwan calls: O Nation of Muhammad, come to al-Rayyan! Whoever is not forgiven in Ramadan, in what month would he be forgiven?! There is no power nor ability except by God."
    ],
    "key_terms": {
      "الريان": "Al-Rayyan - a special gate of Paradise for fasters",
      "رمضان": "Ramadan - the ninth month of the Islamic calendar"
    },
    "seo_question": "What are the rewards for fasting each day of Ramadan?",
